language variant
language en-t800
name t800
gender male 55

// CLASSIC, PRESSED THREE TIMES — the machine from the future.
//
// The third face of the same idea, and the one with no warmth in it at all.
// hal is warm and never emphasises; kitt is bright and emphasises constantly;
// this one is neither, because it is not persuading, reassuring or helping. It
// is stating. The accent lives in voices/en-t800; this file is the body.

// DEEP AND ALMOST MOTIONLESS.
// Lower than hal by a fourth and with barely more range than ancient. It does
// not go as low as OVERLORD (79 Hz) because OVERLORD is authority and this is
// something simpler: mass. 92 -> ~89 Hz, and a range of 14, which is enough to
// not be a drone and not enough to be an opinion.
pitch 90 102

// HEAVY LOW, DEAD TOP. Full through the fundamental octave, and everything above
// 2.5 kHz falls away hard — the opposite of kitt, which lives up there. The 1.4
// kHz point is held up only enough to keep the words: this voice is understood,
// not enjoyed.
tone 190 255 560 215 1400 170 2200 110 3200 60 4000 30

formant 0 102 132 142
formant 1 100 126 136
formant 2 102 116 120
formant 3  98 106 100
formant 4  92  98  80
formant 5  86  90  58
formant 6  76  80  34
formant 7  70  74  22
formant 8  66  70  16

// NO AIR AND NO WAVER. breath is shut — hal's ease is exactly what this lacks —
// and flutter is 0. roughness 2 is the only texture: not the rasp of age, the
// grain of something built.
breath 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
breathw 50 55 60 60 60 60 55 50
// PRESSED, NOT RELAXED. voicing up to 98 and roughness to 3: the folds are held
// hard together, which is what a very low voice sounds like when it is produced
// with effort rather than resonance. The trace of creak that comes with it is
// the point — it is the one thing in this voice that is not smooth, and a
// perfectly smooth version of it sounds like a newsreader who happens to be
// German rather than like something wearing a person.
voicing 98
roughness 3
flutter 0

// Hard consonants, struck rather than released. Where hal articulates patiently
// and kitt articulates quickly, this articulates FLATLY — each one the same
// weight as the last.
consonants 94 86

// A small hard space with nothing soft in it.
echo 34 12

// IT DOES NOT INSIST, BECAUSE IT DOES NOT EXPECT TO BE ARGUED WITH.
// stressAdd is near zero — ancient's doctrine, arrived at from the other
// direction — and stressAmp moves only a little. Nothing is emphasised because
// nothing needs to be.
intonation 3
stressAmp   16 16 17 18 20 23 26 29
stressAdd    0  0  0  0  4  8 14  20
